    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0636" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Food Administrator’s File</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Food Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hoover</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the British Food Controller</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Rhondda</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At a special meeting in Washington to-day 500 leading hotel men from all parts of
                    the country resolved to absolutely abolish the use of wheat products in their
                    hotels until the next harvest in order that through their savings and their
                    example shipments of wheat to the Allies may proceed without interruption.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert Hoover</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
